# C3: the std submodules mlmf-hf-layout may name.
#
# This crate is bytes -> structure. Spec line 90 is explicit that it "never
# enumerates a directory", so there is no `fs`, no `path`, and no `io` here
# and there never should be -- the caller reads the file and hands over the
# bytes.
#
# `error` is present because `ShardError` implements `std::error::Error`,
# which is what lets a consumer put it in a `Box<dyn Error>` alongside
# every other error in the workspace. It was added because the gate
# demanded it, not in advance.
#
# The file exists rather than being absent because `purity.rs::allowed_std`
# panics when a gated member does not declare a list -- an absent file and
# an empty one would otherwise be indistinguishable, and the absent one
# would look like a crate nobody had considered.
error
